{
  "requirement": "requirements.ci.errors",
  "file": "src/evidence.rs",
  "item": "fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]",
  "queries": [
    "early_exits",
    "error_accumulators"
  ],
  "applies": true,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/evidence.rs#fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]` applies. It sequences the repository's checks and holds a local `let mut errors`, so it is a site of `requirements.ci.errors`.\n\n**Violation match.** The only early exit is `fs::canonicalize(root)?` on the first line. It runs before any check and before `errors` exists. Every later check takes `root`, so none can run without it. This is not a failure that skips an independent check, and the match is harmless.\n\n**Continuing after a failure.**\n- A failure of `crate::config::load_workspace_evidence` is pushed to `errors`, and execution continues.\n- `book_source_dir` falls back to `md` after a malformed `book.toml`, so definition collection still runs.\n- `collect_definitions` and `files_with_extension` push errors and `continue` past the failing file or directory.\n- The `validate_setup` failure is pushed to `errors`, and the evidence-file loop still runs.\n- Inside the evidence-file loop, a missing-match error is pushed and `validate_evidence_file` still runs in the same iteration.\n- The coverage check, `discovered_files`, `collect_references_with_progress`, `validate_committed_credentials`, `sites::discover`, `validate_references`, `citations::validate`, `sites::validate` and the two `rust_coverage` validators all run unconditionally and push into the same `errors`.\n\n**No duplicate reports.**\n- `load_workspace_evidence` reads `habeas.toml`.\n- `book_source_dir` reads `book.toml`.\n- `validate_setup` reads `Cargo.toml` and `.config/nextest.toml`.\n- These three checks look at different files, so one failure is not reported twice.\n- `discovery_errors` is a separate list used for a different purpose. It does not duplicate entries within `errors`.\n\nThe site meets its obligations, and no `{fixme}` is needed.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/evidence.rs",
      "item": "fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]",
      "hash": "1ce21a08dc4625f6331cca44c2a588caeb8936e98fbb459f9c97ab169339fb55"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "definition": "requirements.ci.validation_error",
      "text": [
        ":::{definition} validation_error",
        ":phrase: validation error",
        "",
        "One message in a repository validation report, describing a single failed check.",
        "It begins with the affected evidence file, requirement, or source location, names",
        "the failed check, and states the specific missing, invalid, or changed value,",
        "with the expected value when available. It is concise because agents are its",
        "primary readers.",
        ":::"
      ]
